<title>USA: National Computer unit makes acquisition.</title>
<headline>National Computer unit makes acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Computer Systems Inc said Tuesday its 51-percent owned Australian subsidiary, ScanForm NCS, acquired Wells Research Services Pty Ltd of Australia. Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Wells Research, with 1996 revenue of about US$5.7 million, is an independent provider of data collection and processing services to research professionals in small- to medium-sized market research companies.</p>
<p>The combined entity will be known as NCS Australasia Pty Ltd and will be positioned to provide its services in Australia and Asia.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
</text>
